.Dd Septemper 18, 2026
.Dt mclogger 1
.Os mcplex.net
.Sh NAME
.Nm mclogger
.Nd send a log message to mclogd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl P Ar port
.Op Fl p Ar priority
.Cm ident
.Cm message
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
may be used to send a log message to
.Xr mclogd 8 .
.Pp
The following command line options are available:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl P Ar port
Specify the UDP port on which
.Xr mclogd 8
is listening on the loopback interface.  The default is 3737.
.It Fl p Ar priority
Specify the message priority.  The default is \fIuser.info\fR.
.Pp
This is a combination of facility and severity, separated by a dot (.).
.Pp
Valid facility values:
.Bd -literal
    auth      daemon  local0  local3  local6  mail    user
    authpriv  ftp     local1  local4  local7  news    uucp 
    cron      kernel  local2  local5  lpr     syslog
.Ed
.Pp
Valid severity values:
.Bd -literal
    emerg  alert  crit  err  warning  notice  info  debug
.Ed
.It Ar ident
Specify the identifier of the message, typically a program name.
.It Ar message
The message to send.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mclog 1 ,
.Xr mclogd 8
.Sh COPYRIGHT
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel W. McRobb
.Mt dwm@mcplex.net
.Pp

